course: dictionary
lesson: 10447
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Look at the words around it. «The trumpeters are tooting and the soldiers are saluting» is about a marching scene, so trumpeters here are people who play the trumpet.
explain: Read the whole sentence, then ask what would fit. «The trumpeter swan glided across the lake.» A swan cannot play a trumpet, so trumpeter must be the name of a bird. The word swan next to it is your clue.
explain: Big scenes give clues too. «Bang! go the drums! The trumpeters are tooting, and the cannon they are shooting» tells you there is a loud parade with soldiers. A trumpeter in a parade like this is a soldier or herald who sounds signals.
fact: A trumpeter is a person who plays the trumpet.
fact: In the past, a trumpeter could be a soldier or herald who sounded signals on a trumpet.
fact: Trumpeter is also the name of some animals with trumpet-like calls, such as the trumpeter swan.
fact: The trumpeter swan lives in North America and is the largest waterfowl there.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «trumpeter swan» reads as a bird, the meaning is an animal.
exercise: «The trumpeters are tooting and the soldiers are saluting.» Who are the trumpeters in this line? | Motor-cars hooting on the road | *People who play the trumpet | Animals with loud calls | Cannons firing in the battle
exercise: What is a trumpeter swan? | A kind of brass instrument | A king's messenger in a castle | A soldier who carries a flag | *A large bird with a trumpet-like call
exercise: «The trumpeters are tooting and the soldiers are saluting.» What does saluting suggest about the soldiers? | They are asleep in their tents | They are lost in the woods | *They are greeting or honouring someone | They are playing football
test: In history, what was a trumpeter's main job? | To cook the food in the camp | To mend the castle walls | *To sound signals on a trumpet for soldiers | To paint pictures of kings
test: «In bands and orchestras, trumpeters play bright, loud parts.» What does bright, loud suggest about these parts? | Quiet parts that are hard to hear | Parts that are whispered in the dark | *Parts played on the trumpet that stand out clearly | Parts sung softly by children
exam: Which meaning does trumpeter have in «The trumpeter swan glided across the lake»? | A soldier who sounds signals | A person who plays the trumpet | *An animal, a large bird with a trumpet-like call | A herald who reads the news
